{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1486525-requiem-as-a-dark-comedy","id":1486525,"title":"Requiem as a Dark Comedy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-15T09:04:37-07:00","id":1486525,"title":"Requiem as a Dark Comedy","content":"If you were going to run Requiem as a dark comedy and satire, what things would you emphasize, what would you downplay. What tools, hacks or house rules would you use to get the most humor out of the game and the players.<br /> <br /> I want to give this a try in the future and was wondering how other Storytellers would approach this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T09:52:43-07:00","id":1486531,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just me, but the sessions I played and ran (for D&amp;D as well as Requiem) tended to detour into comedy (dark or otherwise) whether I wanted them to or not. <br /> <br /> I suppose discourage physical combat and actually killing anyone (any vampires, that is) and leaning into the &quot;Mean Girls&quot; type of shenanigans in Elysium.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, making it hard to feed on someone without killing them and forcing the players to clean up every death would lead to some gallows humor situations. Like that one scene in Mulholland Drive where the hitman's attempt to escape with the book keeps escalating and he keeps running into potential witnesses. <br /> <br /> Some days, you just can't get rid of a body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T11:57:02-07:00","id":1486538,"title":"","content":"Pretty much a Rockstar game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T13:11:32-07:00","id":1486547,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, I remember someone calling the experience of playing the VtM story &quot;Baptism by Fire&quot; as &quot;Seinfeld with fangs&quot;. After all, when Vampire: The Requiem is played on Tier I and II people and interactions come to forefront. Personal interactions and character catchphrases open for many fun moments. Naturally, VtR is open for dark comedy, which could be interspersed with rather grim moments that cannot be joked away. A nifty example could be Armando Iannucci's film <i>Death of Stalin</i> (2017). Just imagine what happens in the SAS <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/91976/Into-the-Void?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Into the Void</a></b> with that kind of &quot;comedy&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-24-2023, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T13:32:45-07:00","id":1486551,"title":"","content":"I would refine my intentions of what sort of &quot;dark comedy&quot; I was going for. From a practical perspective of things like emphasis, I think the most important part about what kind of black humor to decide on and how that relates to how to stress things in a RPG, is how much the characters are in on the comedy.<br /> <br /> There is a broad spectrum with extremes of the comedy coming from the characters behaving as completely serious despite the situation, the middle ground that stories like <i>Scream</i> hit where the characters are aware of the genre as a source of humor but still subject to it, and dark humor where it only really works because the characters are playing into the humor (Deadpool being a good example of this to its extreme).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T23:33:43-07:00","id":1486594,"title":"","content":"The <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/28026/Blood-Red--Ash-Gray-Vampire-The-Requiem?affiliate_id=321987\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Red+ Ash Gray</a></b> SAS has a brief discussion on how to apply a funny vs. scary theme in that story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","user":"Cabaal","date":". 03-24-2023, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27293-cabaal","name":"Cabaal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27293_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T03:51:35-07:00","id":1486604,"title":"","content":"I always thought that the inherent absurdity of vampires situation would work by itself in making &quot;funny&quot; situations, think about the Sopranos for example, that show is about absolute turds of human beings getting up to all kinds of fuckery and debauchery and manages to be hilarious just for the sheer absurdity of it all, change mobsters with vampires and you have a good chronicle setting for something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T09:51:31-07:00","id":1486637,"title":"","content":"I was thinking one thing I could do is create XP awards that the players could vote on at the end of the session and name them after inspirational characters. Like the &quot;Michael Scott Award&quot; for creating the most awkward or cringiest situation, the &quot;<span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Chrundle</span></span></span> Kelly Award&quot; for most stupiedist or humiliating moment, the &quot;Colin Robinson Award&quot; for causing the most frustrating situation, etc.<br /> Whoever wins the vote gets a bonus beats or xp.<br /> <br /> Also, giving beats out for making the entire table laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:57:36-07:00","id":1486660,"title":"","content":"Vote based XP is usually not a great thing for most tables. Giving everyone some Beats for a great moment of RP, or adding some Beats to the pot if you're using Group Beats, is a way better way to handle that approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}